Quantities, Units and Symbols in Physical Chemistry — IUPAC Green Book (@gc-green: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gc-sources) { r_5SR8CP04E580VSV69MYQNSZ73F
Christopher M. A. Brett and fellow editors for IUPAC. Quantities, Units and Symbols in Physical Chemistry, 4th edition, abridged version. Royal Society of Chemistry, 2023. DOI 10.1039/9781839163180. [IUPAC edition page](https://iupac.org/what-we-do/books/greenbook/) · [Official PDF released March 2025](https://iupac.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/IUPAC-GB4Abridged.pdf).

Read the complete abridged volume during advanced study, returning to the precise quantity definitions for amount, composition, chemical potential, activity, equilibrium, kinetics, and electrochemistry. Distinguish a quantity equation from an equation valid only for particular numerical units. The available PDF has 122 file pages. Its constants table explicitly uses CODATA 2018 information; consult current evaluated constants when a precision claim needs them rather than calling every table value the latest.

IUPAC supplies authorized free PDF access; preserve the actual RSC/IUPAC edition and component notices before reproducing or adapting material. Free access is stated separately from a general redistribution licence. Edition, editors, release information, contents, and availability checked on 29 October 2026. No copy is bundled.

**Return:** [General chemistry sources — books, courses, data, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_37CHT3QSMD33JDMXE59S6M2ME3).

**Fourth chemistry-core inspection — 31 October 2026:** the official abridged PDF was accessible. Selected activity/coefficient and concentration-form equilibrium entries on printed page 50 (PDF page index 61), and pH, ionic activity and the single-ion measurement qualification on printed page 59 (PDF page index 70), were inspected through the extracted text. This bounds the new quantity/reference-concentration discussion; full chemical thermodynamics, electrochemistry and the complete abridged-volume assignment remain. The Gold Book pH endpoint returned HTTP 403, so it is not claimed inspected. Existing edition/copyright and authorized-access qualifications remain; no PDF or table is bundled.


**Fifth chemistry-core inspection — 1 November 2026:** rechecked the official fourth-edition abridged PDF, section 4.13, printed pages 59–60 (PDF indices 70–71): F=eN_A, ionic charge number, electron coefficient, external current and signed cathodic/anodic Faradaic partial currents. The common block explicitly translates its positive reduction-oriented magnitude to the source's negative cathodic-current convention. The neighboring standard/reversible-potential equations are visible reference material, not a derived or applied thermodynamic result in this block. The PDF's constants table identifies its CODATA 2018 basis; no claim is made that all of that table is a current constants adjustment. Exact e and N_A are checked independently against BIPM definitions. Whole sections remain assigned, the authorized free PDF retains its publisher copyright terms, and no source media is bundled.


**Sixth chemistry-core inspection — 1 November 2026:** the official fourth-edition abridged PDF remained accessible. Selected extracted entries on printed pages 49–50 (PDF indices 60–61) were inspected for chemical potential, relative activity, reaction Gibbs energy, affinity, quotient and dimensionless thermodynamic K; printed pages 52–53 (indices 63–64) for standard-state conventions; and printed pages 59–60 (indices 70–71) for electron coefficient, equilibrium potential and current conventions. The common lessons distinguish the dimensionless K used in logarithms from dimensional pressure/concentration constants. They derive reaction and cell normalization with the stated work signs. Exact R=N_Ak_B and F=N_Ae products agree with the defining constants listed on PDF index 1; other table entries retain their stated CODATA 2018 basis. This is a bounded entry inspection, not a whole-volume or every-table audit. Authorized access and publisher/component rights remain; no PDF or table is bundled.

